Cut Amazon-era legacy + fix bugs Cookie flagged

Two passes in one commit because they were tangled:

## Cleanup -- remove unused legacy

The portable Tiramisu CLI does not use the old multi-agent dispatch /
knowledge-indexing / queue runner systems. They lived as dead weight,
broke `t scan` reports with noise, and confused new readers about what
the system actually is.

Deleted:
- second_brain/ (entire dir: brain, cli, memory, reranker, user_profile,
  index_personalization, kb_report, test_kb_hits, type_config)
- queue/ (runner.py, queue.json, state.json) -- Amazon-era task queue
- ingest-ide-sessions/, ingest-repos/ -- Rust subprojects for old session
  log ingestion
- knowledge/, logs/ -- empty placeholder dirs
- hooks/auto_index.py, check_candidates.py, load_memories.py,
  ingest_sessions.py -- all called the old second_brain CLI
- scripts/fetch_github_trending.py, ingest_gentoomen.py,
  extract_session_learnings.py -- orphaned utilities depending on
  the old indexing pipeline
- setup.sh, setup.ps1, schema.sql, tiramisu.db -- old install +
  schema for tables we don't use
- agent-architecture.md, agent-config-template.md, memory-system.md,
  github-publishing-plan.md -- Amazon-era design docs

Rewrote (planned but not yet wired into CLI):
- agents/brioche.md  (HR / agent creator)
- agents/cannoli.md  (researcher)
- agents/mochi.md    (brainstorm)
  All stripped of second_brain memory protocols and Amazon-era table
  references. Each marked "planned -- not yet wired into the t CLI."

## Bug fixes Cookie flagged in t scan

scripts/llm.py
- _load_env(): wrap file read in try/except. Crashing on corrupted .env
  meant zero-output failures on every t invocation.
- Document the FAST_MODEL vs DEFAULT_MODEL distinction (cost/latency vs
  quality tier).
- Document the prompt-caching tradeoff in invoke / invoke_stream.

scripts/learn.py
- categorize(): narrow the bare except; log the failure to stderr so
  silent miscategorization is debuggable.

hooks/eclair_post_commit.py
- Replace bare except with FileNotFoundError/OSError. The previous
  catch-all swallowed KeyboardInterrupt and would hide real breakage.
- Empty commit message branch now logs to stderr instead of silently
  exiting.

Net diff: 4500+ lines removed, ~60 added.

